"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h2>Test Scenarios</h2>\n<p>✅ Test scenarios generated</p>\n<p>To generate comprehensive test scenarios, we first define the underlying Finite State Machine (FSM) structure based on the <strong>User Authentication Flow</strong>.</p>\n<h3><strong>FSM State Reference</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>S1: Logged Out</strong> (Initial)</li>\n<li><strong>S2: Login Initiated</strong> (Transient)</li>\n<li><strong>S3: MFA Pending</strong> (Normal)</li>\n<li><strong>S4: Authenticated</strong> (Normal/Stable)</li>\n<li><strong>S5: Authentication Failed</strong> (Error/Transient)</li>\n<li><strong>S6: Account Locked</strong> (Error/Terminal)</li>\n<li><strong>S7: Password Reset Required</strong> (Normal/Transient)</li>\n<li><strong>S8: Session Expired</strong> (Error/Transient)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3><strong>Test Scenarios</strong></h3>\n<h4><strong>1. Happy Path: Standard Single-Factor Authentication</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Successful Password-Only Login</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S1: Logged Out</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit valid credentials (MFA disabled)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S1] → (Submit Credentials) → [S4: Authenticated]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User is granted access to the dashboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates the most common successful entry point for users without multi-factor requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>2. Happy Path: Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) Flow</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Successful MFA Login</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S1: Logged Out</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit valid credentials (MFA enabled)</li>\n<li>Submit valid MFA TOTP code</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S1] → (Submit Credentials) → [S3: MFA Pending]</li>\n<li>[S3] → (Submit Valid MFA) → [S4: Authenticated]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User reaches Authenticated state after two-step verification.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates the transition through transient security states.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>3. Error Path: Brute Force Protection (Account Lockout)</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Account Lockout on Repeated Failures</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S1: Logged Out</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit invalid credentials (Attempt 1)</li>\n<li>Submit invalid credentials (Attempt 2)</li>\n<li>Submit invalid credentials (Attempt 3 - Threshold)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S1] → (Invalid Creds) → [S5: Authentication Failed]</li>\n<li>[S5] → (Invalid Creds) → [S5: Authentication Failed]</li>\n<li>[S5] → (Invalid Creds) → [S6: Account Locked]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> Final state is Account Locked; further login attempts are rejected.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates security constraints and error state transitions for brute-force mitigation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>4. Error Path: MFA Verification Failure</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Invalid MFA Code Handling</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S3: MFA Pending</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit incorrect MFA code</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S3] → (Invalid MFA) → [S5: Authentication Failed]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User is redirected back to the failure state or login screen.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Ensures that valid primary credentials do not bypass the need for a valid secondary factor.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>5. Boundary Test: Session Expiration during Active Use</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Session Timeout Transition</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S4: Authenticated</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>System idle exceeds <code>session_timeout</code></li>\n<li>User attempts to click &quot;Refresh Profile&quot;</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S4] → (Clock Tick/Timeout) → [S8: Session Expired]</li>\n<li>[S8] → (Any Action) → [S1: Logged Out]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User is forcibly moved to Logged Out state and prompted to re-authenticate.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates the temporal boundary of the Authenticated state.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>6. State Coverage: Forced Password Change</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Expired Password Redirection</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S1: Logged Out</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit valid credentials (Password flagged as expired)</li>\n<li>Submit new password matching policy</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S1] → (Submit Credentials) → [S7: Password Reset Required]</li>\n<li>[S7] → (Update Password) → [S1: Logged Out] (or S4 depending on policy)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User is blocked from S4 until S7 requirements are met.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Exercises the &quot;Password Reset Required&quot; state to ensure compliance with credential rotation policies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>7. Transition Coverage: Manual Logout from Authenticated State</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Intentional Session Termination</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S4: Authenticated</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Click &quot;Logout&quot; button</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S4] → (Logout Event) → [S1: Logged Out]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> Session tokens are invalidated and user returns to initial state.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates the clean exit transition from a stable state back to the initial state.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>8. Boundary Test: MFA Token Replay/Reuse</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> MFA Code Reuse Prevention</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S3: MFA Pending</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Submit valid MFA code (Success)</li>\n<li>(In a parallel session) Submit the same MFA code again</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S3] → (Submit MFA) → [S4: Authenticated]</li>\n<li>[S3] → (Submit Reused MFA) → [S5: Authentication Failed]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> The second attempt with the same code fails.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates the &quot;one-time&quot; invariant of the MFA transition.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>9. Error Path: Invalid State Transition (Direct URL Access)</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Unauthorized State Access Attempt</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S1: Logged Out</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Attempt to access <code>/dashboard</code> (S4) directly via URL</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S1] → (Unauthorized Access Attempt) → [S1: Logged Out]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> System remains in S1; user is redirected to login.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Validates that the machine cannot jump to S4 without passing through S2/S3.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>10. Transition Coverage: Recovery from Failed State</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scenario Name:</strong> Retry after Failed Attempt</li>\n<li><strong>Initial State:</strong> S5: Authentication Failed</li>\n<li><strong>Event Sequence:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Click &quot;Try Again&quot;</li>\n<li>Submit valid credentials</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected States:</strong>\n<ol>\n<li>[S5] → (Retry) → [S1: Logged Out]</li>\n<li>[S1] → (Submit Valid Creds) → [S4: Authenticated]</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> User successfully authenticates after a previous failure.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Ensures the system resets correctly from an error state to allow for a fresh attempt.</li>\n</ul>\n</div></div><div><div class=\"spinner-border\" role=\"status\"><span class=\"sr-only\">Loading...</span></div></div>"